The WebAssembly modules in internal/modules/authorizer and
internal/modules/analysis are compiled from rust/ and contain third-party
code:

Cedar (https://github.com/cedar-policy/cedar)
Copyright Cedar Contributors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The modules contain the crates cedar-policy 4.13.0, cedar-policy-core 4.13.0,
cedar-policy-formatter 4.13.0 and cedar-policy-symcc 0.7.0.

cedar-policy-symcc 0.7.0 is modified. rust/vendor/cedar-policy-symcc-0.7.0
removes LocalSolver and the solver pool from wasm targets, because tokio's
process feature does not build there. The change is in
rust/patches/cedar-policy-symcc-0.7.0-wasm.patch, and each changed file
carries a notice.

The modules also contain other Rust crates under the Apache-2.0, MIT and
Unicode-3.0 licenses. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt lists each crate with the
full text of its license.

This product does not include an SMT solver. Package analysis runs a solver
executable that the user provides, such as cvc5.
